\end{align*}
The function  $h$ is continuous. Moreover, $[a,b\vee m]^{\ensuremath{k}}$ is a compact and convex subset of~$\mathbb{R}^k$. We can thus apply  Brouwer's fixed-point theorem to deduce that 
\begin{align*}
\lambda=2g'(\,\normtwo{\textcolor{black}{\ensuremath{Y}}-\textcolor{black}{\ensuremath{X}}\ensuremath{\widehat \beta}^{\lambda}}^2)\left(\textcolor{black}{\ensuremath{c}}_1\,\norm{(\textcolor{black}{\ensuremath{X}} P_1\ensuremath{M}_1^{+})^\top\textcolor{black}{\ensuremath{\varepsilon}}}_{q_1}^*,\dots,\textcolor{black}{\ensuremath{c}}_k\,\norm{(\textcolor{black}{\ensuremath{X}} P_k\ensuremath{M}_k^{+})^\top\textcolor{black}{\ensuremath{\varepsilon}}}_{q_k}^*\right)^\top
